1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,840
What if science class felt like your favourite game?

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,840
Drop an object into water.

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,840
Guide the rain through a city.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,640
Balance a lever.

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:15,340
Every move is real science.

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:24,097
This is İDÜ Lab: free science games from Izmir Demokrasi University.

7
00:00:32,842 --> 00:00:35,482
But for many students, science looks like this.

8
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:38,082
Read about it.

9
00:00:38,142 --> 00:00:40,682
Memorise the formula.

10
00:00:40,742 --> 00:00:43,282
Find the one right answer.

11
00:00:43,342 --> 00:00:47,082
And whatever you do, don’t get it wrong.

12
00:00:47,142 --> 00:00:53,682
No wonder so many decide, far too early: science is not for me.

13
00:00:53,742 --> 00:00:56,882
That’s not a student problem.

14
00:00:56,942 --> 00:01:00,707
That’s a design problem.

15
00:01:01,317 --> 00:01:02,957
So we redesigned it.

16
00:01:03,017 --> 00:01:05,157
You don’t start with the answer.

17
00:01:05,217 --> 00:01:08,657
You start with a guess: where should the weight go?

18
00:01:08,717 --> 00:01:11,557
Try it, and the lever shows you what happened.

19
00:01:11,617 --> 00:01:12,657
Not level yet?

20
00:01:12,717 --> 00:01:15,857
Adjust and try again.

21
00:01:15,917 --> 00:01:16,957
Level!

22
00:01:17,017 --> 00:01:20,757
You solved it, and now you know why.

23
00:01:20,817 --> 00:01:21,757
Prediction.

24
00:01:21,817 --> 00:01:22,757
Experiment.

25
00:01:22,817 --> 00:01:24,357
Observation.

26
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:28,357
That’s not a trick to make science sweeter.

27
00:01:28,417 --> 00:01:33,357
It’s exactly how scientists work.

28
00:01:33,417 --> 00:01:41,385
Here, the game is the experiment.

29
00:01:41,995 --> 00:01:43,635
And the science is real.

30
00:01:43,695 --> 00:01:48,735
Every board runs on true equations: the lever balances only when the moments match.

31
00:01:48,795 --> 00:01:56,835
Change the launch angle, and the ball follows a real projectile path.

32
00:01:56,895 --> 00:02:02,735
Physics you can see, and steer.

33
00:02:02,795 --> 00:02:17,995
Measure one mountain and one horizon, and you can work out the size of the whole Earth, just as al-Biruni did a thousand years ago.

34
00:02:18,605 --> 00:02:20,445
Every level follows the same five steps.

35
00:02:20,505 --> 00:02:21,745
Predict.

36
00:02:21,805 --> 00:02:23,045
Try.

37
00:02:23,105 --> 00:02:24,345
See.

38
00:02:24,405 --> 00:02:25,645
Explain.

39
00:02:25,705 --> 00:02:27,245
Transfer.

40
00:02:27,305 --> 00:02:31,845
One rule: the answer appears only after you solve the level.

41
00:02:31,905 --> 00:02:34,845
Then the game asks: what if the distance changed?

42
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:38,045
Predict first, then see.

43
00:02:38,105 --> 00:02:41,745
Explain it in your own words.

44
00:02:41,805 --> 00:02:44,845
Nobody hands you the answer.

45
00:02:44,905 --> 00:02:50,537
The discovery is yours.

46
00:02:51,147 --> 00:02:52,687
And it’s for everyone.

47
00:02:52,747 --> 00:02:57,387
It’s free, it runs in the browser, and it speaks twenty-five languages.

48
00:02:57,447 --> 00:03:05,287
Switch the language and the lab switches with you: English, Kazakh, Georgian, Arabic and more.

49
00:03:05,347 --> 00:03:12,187
The same games and the same levels, for every learner.

50
00:03:12,247 --> 00:03:19,012
No download needed: it runs on a phone, a laptop or a classroom smart board.

51
00:03:19,622 --> 00:03:22,862
Science also has a history, and a home.

52
00:03:22,922 --> 00:03:27,362
Solve equations on Al-Khwarizmi’s balance.

53
00:03:27,422 --> 00:03:35,362
Find your city’s latitude from one shadow, in Ulugh Beg’s observatory.

54
00:03:35,422 --> 00:03:43,362
Keep a yurt warm through a winter night.

55
00:03:43,422 --> 00:03:45,862
Plan every move in Mangala.

56
00:03:45,922 --> 00:03:51,554
Every game connects the science to the people and cultures behind it.

57
00:03:52,164 --> 00:03:53,204
And teachers?

58
00:03:53,264 --> 00:03:54,904
They get a complete toolkit.

59
00:03:54,964 --> 00:04:01,104
Run a live class or a team competition, or put a level on the smart board.

60
00:04:01,164 --> 00:04:08,304
Open a ready-made lesson in seconds.

61
00:04:08,364 --> 00:04:20,029
And with the Science Passport, every skill a learner masters can become a signed, verifiable badge.

62
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:29,779
From pattern puzzles in primary school to epsilon–delta proofs at university.

63
00:04:29,839 --> 00:04:30,579
More than 150 games.

64
00:04:30,639 --> 00:04:31,379
More than 3,000 levels.

65
00:04:31,439 --> 00:04:37,479
Twenty-five languages.

66
00:04:37,539 --> 00:04:38,879
So, why gamify science?

67
00:04:38,939 --> 00:04:40,879
Because curiosity is the best teacher.

68
00:04:40,939 --> 00:04:46,470
And every learner deserves a lab.

